{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:f564d2fc9c61c474","name":"K-X12 Probe Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-f564d2fc9c61c474","title":"K-X12 Probe Droid","revision":19199,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:30:48Z","sha256":"ea5173c2e0c1ba596958f100b0c423ae7aed64356771bb9a44715228aac2a28c","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19199","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=K-X12%20Probe%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-f564d2fc9c61c474","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Though officially billed as a Probe Droid, the K-X12 model Droid from ",{"tag":"a","children":["MerenData"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/MerenData","referenceId":"reference:c09d29dd0bc8cb90"}," becomes popular because of its ability to fulfill multiple roles. The hovering Droid is good at getting into and out of dangerous or confined locales, and its three clawed ",{"tag":"a","children":["Appendages"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Appendages"}," allow it to twist, move, and otherwise manipulate objects that would block other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"},". Though ",{"tag":"a","children":["MerenData"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/MerenData","referenceId":"reference:c09d29dd0bc8cb90"}," claims that the blaster is used only to clear away debris, owners of K-X12 Probe Droids use them as Security and Patrol Droids because of their offensive capabilities.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["MerenData's Probe Droids come into widespread use during ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi Civil War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi_Civil_War"},", when ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic","referenceId":"reference:6517b7e15507b001"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith_Empire","referenceId":"reference:303e4cc32aa1a8e1"},", and private citizens alike use the Droids for security and observation. Many of the Droids are reprogrammed and sent out as Espionage Droids, slipping into enemy facilities through unusual points of entry. These Probe Droids are loaded into hollowed-out ",{"tag":"a","children":["Concussion Missiles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Concussion_Missiles","referenceId":"reference:c95ee0f6eb24f16e"}," and fired into the atmosphere of enemy-controlled planets; the Droid is programmed to destroy the missile from the inside before impact, then float away to avoid slamming into the planet.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["K-X12 Probe Droids can't be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["K-X12 Probe Droid Statistics (CL 2)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Small ",{"tag":"a","children":["4th-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/4th-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 3/",{"tag":"a","children":["Scout"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scout","referenceId":"reference:8a1db462be753774"}," 1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +4; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Low-Light Vision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Low-Light_Vision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +1